!! Cellular Distortions

Kalamazoo College senior year work (SIP).

* Macro film photographs of cell phones, when cell phones were new, or at least newly ubiquitous objects
* Adobe Illustrator: digital "painting" from the photos
* Large-format inkjet plotter: a new tool to try ("why not!?")

!! The Flip-Flop

The piece only existed because I kept translating the work from medium to medium, tool to tool, format to format. [[Robin Sloan]] calls this process [[the flip-flop|Dancing the Flip-Flop]]:

<<<
flip-flop (n.): the process of pushing a work of art or craft from the physical world to the digital world and back, often more than once.
<<< Robin Sloan

How it went: film photography of actual cell phones → scanned into the computer → processed a bit → brought into Illustrator → vector "paintings" made from the photos → hugely upscaled and printed on a large-format inkjet onto light-box frosted transparencies → mounted on a custom-built four-sided physical lightbox, hung (seemingly magically floating) in the middle of a gallery space.

Physical, digital, digital, physical, physical…

